{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/10","id":4949058377,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABJvyjSQ","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/10","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/10.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/10.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/10","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/10/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/10/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/10/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/statuses/f578ffdf5e1d3b17e3bcfe92e6d42af7743e4fed","number":10,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Link networks with the zero link on the grid, problem solving diagram fixes, network gallery in Research, cleaner ecosystem","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #9\n\nEach item of the issue is listed below with its solution and the test that checks it. The full analysis is in the\ncase study [`docs/case-studies/issue-9/README.md`](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/README.md).\nIt covers the timeline, a requirement → solution → test table, root causes, research and debug tools.\n\n## Link networks\n\n- **Encoding with the zero link.** 0 is \"nothing\". A network of N links is 2N digits in base N + 1, so there are\n  (N + 1)^(2N) networks: one link gives 00₂, 10₂, 01₂, 11₂; two links run 00₃ 00₃ … 22₃ 22₃ (81); three links give\n  4,096 and four links 390,625. Grouping by renaming links leaves 4 / 45 / 720 / 16,900 classes (Burnside), and a brute\n  force in `experiments/count-networks.mjs` gives the same counts.\n- **Drawing.** Each link is one continuous Bézier curve in its own colour: a bar at the source, then its own middle,\n  then an arrow at the target. Nothing breaks the line in the middle. Self-references are symmetric, so (1: 1 1) is a\n  figure eight (∞), also inside larger networks. Tests check that every network is drawable, that tangents are\n  continuous, that the figures are symmetric, and that ends touch the middles they refer to.\n- **Gallery.** \"Every configuration of 1–4 links\" is now on the Research page as well as Art. It shows the formula and\n  base subscripts, every network page by page, or one per class.\n- **Random network on click.** Clicking a network symbol shows a random network, with small labels for the math\n  notation and the links notation.\n- **Rain on the grid.** Exactly two symbol columns per 64 px grid cell, starting at the grid lines. The rain drives the\n  grid drift, so the two never slide apart.\n\n![gallery](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/screenshots/after-network-gallery.png?raw=true)\n![random network](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/screenshots/after-meta-theory-random-network.png?raw=true)\n![rain on the grid](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/screenshots/after-rain-on-grid-debug.png?raw=true)\n\n## Universal problem solving\n\n- **Layout.** Labels have fixed widths (`textLength`), and nodes and arrows are placed from those widths. The \"S\" of\n  \"Solution\" was hidden behind the final node (825.6–960 against 819–841), and \"decomposition\" ran into its arrow\n  (281.9 > 280). The measurements are in `data/psd-old-overlaps.txt`. A test checks that no label touches another\n  label, a node or an arrow.\n- **Caption.** It now only links the original drawing and konard/problem-solving.\n- **Method notes.** They explain recursion and applying the algorithm to itself (a plan, or an algorithm when the\n  decomposition is deep enough). They describe going back to the formulation as self-improvement that rarely means\n  starting over (\"make requirements less dumb\"), and link to the implementations in link-assistant/hive-mind and\n  link-assistant/formal-ai.\n\n![diagram](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/screenshots/after-problem-solving-diagram.png?raw=true)\n![notes](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/screenshots/after-problem-solving-notes.png?raw=true)\n\n## Repositories, menu and experience\n\n- **Hidden organizations.** EfficiencyParadigm, Qvinciy, Gls-full, links-games, open-online-tools,\n  Svetozar-Technologies and meteor-shuttler are hidden everywhere: owners, projects, picks and packages.\n- **Empty repositories and broken forks.** They are detected automatically from facts collected by\n  `experiments/collect-repository-health.cjs` (`--verbose`):\n  - konard/TheAnime is empty: only a LICENSE and a 61-byte README.\n  - konard/slava is a broken fork: its root commit is by another person and predates the repository, and the original\n    is not public.\n- **Totals.** Not shown: 32 repositories of hidden organizations, 63 empty, 26 broken forks, 1 deleted.\n- **No \"client copies\".** Only forks of public projects are shown (3, each with \"Fork of …\"). Nothing is stored or\n  shown about copies of non-public projects (86): the collector records only `public: false`.\n- **Menu.** The order is now CV, Experience, Repositories.\n- **Experience \"All\".** It shows every profession with every listed repository.\n- **Scientist.** \"Researcher\" is renamed \"Scientist\".\n\n![kinds](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/screenshots/after-repositories-kinds.png?raw=true)\n![experience all](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-9-5afd78997696/docs/case-studies/issue-9/screenshots/after-experience-all-examples.png?raw=true)\n\n## External issues\n\nkonard/links-visuals already draws each link as one path in its own colour. The defects came from this site's own\nrenderer (from issue #7), and they are fixed here. No external project is at fault, so no issue was filed (see\nsection 6 of the case study).\n\n## How to reproduce and verify\n\nThe before-state is shown by the issue screenshots in `docs/case-studies/issue-9/images`. To verify:\n\n```sh\nnpm ci\nnpm run check     # eslint, prettier, line limit, secretlint\nnpm run test:ci   # 8 files, 128 tests\nnode experiments/repository-health-rules.cjs   # what is hidden and why\nnode experiments/count-networks.mjs            # network counts by brute force\n```\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T09:01:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T15:43:37Z","closed_at":"2026-10-21T15:43:37Z","merged_at":"2026-10-21T15:43:37Z","merge_commit_sha":"e49352c4b2eae6003ea2a3f5f9d7a90b93035722","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avata